; Interprets: RFC 5778
;; What RFC 5778's clauses state in prose about an AVP's value or presence,
;; read by hand and pinned to the sentences read (docs/constraints.md), in
;; clause order. A block on the DER or DEA binds the document's print of
;; them under MIP6I (7), one on the MIR or MIA its print under MIP6A (8),
;; neither shared by another document's print of a command; a block with no
;; scope, or within a grouped AVP, holds wherever a document reading the
;; AVP reads it (docs/constraints.md, Precedence). What the home agent
;; learnt from the Binding Update or IKE exchange, and what the Diameter
;; server assigned, the messages do not show, so a rule resting on them is
;; `text-only`.


;; The MN-NAI mobility option of the Binding Update, outside the message.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: mir-user-name-the-mn-nai
; AVP: User-Name
; Command: MIP6-Request
; Section: 4.2
"The HA MUST copy the MN-NAI mobility option value to the User-Name AVP in the subsequent request messages."
    text-only


;; AUTHORIZE_AUTHENTICATE is RFC 6733's value 3.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: der-auth-request-type-authorize-authenticate
; AVP: Auth-Request-Type
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Request
; Section: 5.1.1
"Thus, the Auth-Request-Type AVP MUST be set to the value AUTHORIZE_AUTHENTICATE."
    range 3


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: mia-success-mip-mobile-node-address
; AVP: MIP-Mobile-Node-Address
; Command: MIP6-Answer
; Section: 5.2.2
"An MIA message with the Result-Code AVP set to DIAMETER_SUCCESS MUST include the MIP-Mobile-Node-Address AVP."
    present-if Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS


;; MIP6_AUTH_MN_AAA is the one value section 6.20 defines.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: mir-mn-aaa-mip-mn-aaa-spi
; AVP: MIP-MN-AAA-SPI
; Command: MIP6-Request
; Section: 6.3
"When the MIP6-Auth-Mode AVP is set to value MIP6_AUTH_MN_AAA, this AVP MUST be present in the MIR message."
    present-if MIP6-Auth-Mode = MIP6_AUTH_MN_AAA


;; The answer's MIP-MN-HA-MSA, against the MIR's MIP6-Auth-Mode, which the
;; MIA does not carry; read on the MIA through a path into it. Whether the
;; MIP-MN-HA-MSA is "valid" is the server's.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: mia-mn-aaa-mip-mn-ha-spi
; AVP: MIP-MN-HA-MSA
; Command: MIP6-Answer
; Section: 6.4
"When the MIP6-Auth-Mode AVP is set to value MIP6_AUTH_MN_AAA, and the Diameter server returns a valid MIP-MN-HA-MSA AVP in the MIA message, this AVP MUST be present inside the MIP-MN-HA-MSA AVP."
    absent-if request/MIP6-Auth-Mode = MIP6_AUTH_MN_AAA and not MIP-MN-HA-MSA/MIP-MN-HA-SPI


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: mip-mobile-node-address-family
; AVP: MIP-Mobile-Node-Address
; Section: 6.5
"The MIP-Mobile-Node-Address AVP (AVP Code 333) is of type Address and contains the HA assigned IPv6 or IPv4 home address of the mobile node."
    encoding ip-address


;; What the server assigned, a prefix or an address, the answer does not
;; say.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: mia-mip-mobile-node-address-prefix-only
; AVP: MIP-Mobile-Node-Address
; Command: MIP6-Answer
; Section: 6.5
"If the Diameter server assigns only an IPv6 home network prefix to the mobile node, the lower 64 bits of the MIP-Mobile-Node-Address AVP provided address MUST be set to zero."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: mip-careof-address-family
; AVP: MIP-Careof-Address
; Section: 6.7
"The MIP-Careof-Address AVP (AVP Code 487) is of type Address and contains the IPv6 or the IPv4 care-of address of the mobile node."
    encoding ip-address


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: mir-mn-aaa-mip-authenticator
; AVP: MIP-Authenticator
; Command: MIP6-Request
; Section: 6.8
"When the MIP6-Auth-Mode AVP is set to value MIP6_AUTH_MN_AAA, this AVP MUST be present in the MIR message."
    present-if MIP6-Auth-Mode = MIP6_AUTH_MN_AAA


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: mir-mn-aaa-mip-mac-mobility-data
; AVP: MIP-MAC-Mobility-Data
; Command: MIP6-Request
; Section: 6.9
"When the MIP6-Auth-Mode AVP is set to value MIP6_AUTH_MN_AAA, this AVP MUST be present in the MIR message."
    present-if MIP6-Auth-Mode = MIP6_AUTH_MN_AAA


;; "None" (1), no replay protection.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: mip-replay-mode-default
; AVP: MIP-Replay-Mode
; Within: MIP-MN-HA-MSA
; Section: 6.12
"The absence of the MIP-Replay-Mode AVP MUST be treated as no replay protection was selected."
    default None


;; As section 6.4's.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: mia-mn-aaa-mip-algorithm-type
; AVP: MIP-MN-HA-MSA
; Command: MIP6-Answer
; Section: 6.13
"When the MIP6-Auth-Mode AVP is set to value MIP6_AUTH_MN_AAA, and the Diameter server returns a valid MIP-MN-HA-MSA AVP in the MIA message, this AVP MUST be present inside the MIP-MN-HA-MSA AVP."
    absent-if request/MIP6-Auth-Mode = MIP6_AUTH_MN_AAA and not MIP-MN-HA-MSA/MIP-Algorithm-Type


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: mip-timestamp-octets
; AVP: MIP-Timestamp
; Section: 6.16
"The MIP-Timestamp AVP (AVP Code 490) is of type OctetString and contains an 8-octet timestamp value (i.e., 64-bit timestamp) from the Mobility message replay protection option, defined in [RFC4285]."
    length 8 octets


;; AUTHORIZE_AUTHENTICATE is RFC 6733's value 3. The section's
;; DIAMETER_ERROR_AUTH_MODE, a server's answer, is section 7.2's
;; DIAMETER_ERROR_MIP6_AUTH_MODE (5041).
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: mir-mn-aaa-auth-request-type
; AVP: Auth-Request-Type
; Command: MIP6-Request
; Section: 6.20
"When the MIP6-Auth_Mode AVP is set to the value of MIP6_AUTH_MN_AAA, the Auth-Request-Type AVP MUST be set to the value of AUTHORIZE_AUTHENTICATE."
    values 3 if MIP6-Auth-Mode = MIP6_AUTH_MN_AAA


;; The coupled accounting model's Accounting-Request, RFC 6733's, which the
;; document lists the AVP for and does not print; whether the home agent
;; has the identity is the node's.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: acr-chargeable-user-identity-if-available
; AVP: Chargeable-User-Identity
; Section: 6.21
"This AVP MUST be included if it is available in the home agent."
    text-only


;; Table 8.1's DER column: what its "0" says the Diameter-EAP-Request never
;; carries, an AVP its body admits only through * [ AVP ]. The table's
;; other cells against the bodies: the DER's MIP6-Agent-Info "1" and
;; MIP-Mobile-Node-Address "1-2", where section 5.1.1's body prints them
;; optional and only the first DER carries them, and the MIA's
;; MIP-MSA-Lifetime "1", an AVP the body holds only within MIP-MN-HA-MSA,
;; are read by no block (docs/constraints.md).
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: der-mip-mn-aaa-spi-table-absent
; AVP: MIP-MN-AAA-SPI
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Request
; Section: 8.1
"0:"
"The AVP MUST NOT be present in the message."
"MIP-MN-AAA-SPI | 0 | 0 | 0-1 | 0 |"
    absent


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: der-mip-mn-ha-spi-table-absent
; AVP: MIP-MN-HA-SPI
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Request
; Section: 8.1
"0:"
"The AVP MUST NOT be present in the message."
"MIP-MN-HA-SPI | 0 | 0 | 0-1 | 0 |"
    absent


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: der-mip-careof-address-table-absent
; AVP: MIP-Careof-Address
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Request
; Section: 8.1
"0:"
"The AVP MUST NOT be present in the message."
"MIP-Careof-Address | 0 | 0 | 0-1 | 0 |"
    absent


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: der-mip-authenticator-table-absent
; AVP: MIP-Authenticator
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Request
; Section: 8.1
"0:"
"The AVP MUST NOT be present in the message."
"MIP-Authenticator | 0 | 0 | 0-1 | 0 |"
    absent


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: der-mip-mac-mobility-data-table-absent
; AVP: MIP-MAC-Mobility-Data
